-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f0706abc-4e66-52f8-b5c0-361f47fd6f02
-- title:
--   All-layer smooth-point stalks from base-layer stalks, shared ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\bar F$ denotes `fieldBar q M'` — the subfield `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` of the Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, obtained by base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` (the kernel of the reduction map on unit groups attached to `dvd_sq_mul q M'`) — and $\kappa$ denotes the residue field of $A$.
--
--   *Arithmetic frame.* Fixed are a prime $q$ with $5\le q$ (`hq`), a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the subfield of the Laurent series over $\kappa$ generated by the $q$-expansion `jqModC κ` of $j$ and by its $M'$-fold substitution `jqNModC κ M'`) is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa\to w$'s residue field is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which the value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ M')$ lies in `ssJSet q κ`; a distinguished element $s$ of $W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into $\bar F$. Also fixed is a datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, with the membership criterion and residue compatibility for constants from $A$, the scaling property for nonzero elements, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with the pushforward of divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` demands that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *The small field $k_0$.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ is fixed, together with $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), and the valuation subring $A\cap k_0=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is assumed to be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), and with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary data.* A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`); an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ (`hζ₀`); an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hϖtA`) such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   *Layers.* A type $\iota$ indexes a family $K$ of intermediate fields of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ characterised by $x\in A_n\iff x\in A$ (`hAn`); a base layer $K_b$ with $K_b=\bot$, i.e. $K_b=k_0$ (`hKb`), carries a valuation subring $A_b$ with the same characterisation (`hAb`) and a generator $\varpi_b\ne 0$ of its maximal ideal (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   The conclusion is formulated with $k_0$ acting on $\bar F$ through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and asserts the following for all intermediate fields $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ and all valuation subrings $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying: the generation hypothesis that `IntermediateField.adjoin ↥k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(fieldBar q M'))) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`; and the linear disjointness hypothesis that for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-field generated by the image of $K'$, linear independence of $c$ over $K'$ together with $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ (the $c_i$ taken in $\bar F$) forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$. Further quantified over are a field $FSS$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\bar F$ to $FSS$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $\bar F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism to $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ and its residue map on constants, and with the scaling property for nonzero elements) such that an element of $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` precisely when it lies in $W_0$; and a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ (the ends), a family $S_b$ of subrings of $\bar F$, families $\varphi_b(Q):\mathrm{Polynomial}\,A_b\to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q):S_b(Q)\to\kappa$ of ring homomorphisms, and a family $D_b$ of sets of places of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   *Hypothesis on the base-layer data.* It is assumed that $\#N=q+1$ and that for every place $Q\notin N$ the following twelve clauses hold: the image in $\bar F$ of every $a\in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ equals that image; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X))=0$; $S_b(Q)$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the kernel of $\chi_b(Q)$; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in the compositum $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of }K_b)\sqcup F_0$; every element $f$ of that compositum satisfies $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_b(Q)$ with $h\ne0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; all elements of $S_b(Q)$ lie in `R.integers`, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` exactly when it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f\in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)f$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ which are rational, for which every $f\in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_b(Q)f=0$. In addition: the discs are pairwise disjoint ($Q,Q'\notin N$ and $P\in D_b(Q)\cap D_b(Q')$ imply $Q=Q'$); they avoid the cusps, in that for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_b(Q)$ the order at $P$ of the image in $\bar F$ under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $\ge 0$; and they are equivariant: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of $\bar F$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and for every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N$ under its action on places, and for $Q\notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Db Q) = Db (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Under these hypotheses there exist families $S_n(Q,n)$ of subrings of $\bar F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q,n):\mathrm{Polynomial}\,A_n\to S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n):S_n(Q,n)\to\kappa$, and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, such that $\#N=q+1$ (the same end set) and, for every $Q\notin N$, the following hold.
--
--   For every layer $n$: the map sending $a\in A_n$ to the residue in $\kappa$ of its image in $A$ is surjective; the image in $\bar F$ of every $a\in A_n$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))=0$; for every $c\in A_n$ whose residue in $\kappa$ vanishes there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_n(Q,n)\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A_n$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_n(Q,n)f$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))=c$; for every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ the element lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and its residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)f$ in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; $D_n(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ at which every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ is regular with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ iff $\chi_n(Q,n)f=0$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)\ne\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_n$; $S_n(Q,n)$ is a local ring in which membership in the maximal ideal is equivalent to vanishing under $\chi_n(Q,n)$, and is Noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in the compositum $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of }K_n)\sqcup F_0$, and every element $f$ of that compositum satisfies $f\cdot h=g$ with $g,h\in S_n(Q,n)$, $h\ne0$; the linear disjointness clause holds for $K_n$ in the same shape as the hypothesis above (elements of the compositum that are annihilated by a relation with $K_n$-linearly independent coefficients from $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ all vanish); for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_n(Q,n)\to A_n$ satisfying the two normalisations $\chi\circ\varphi_n(Q,n)\circ C=\mathrm{id}$ and residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_n(Q,n)f$, the kernel of $\chi$ is generated by $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)-\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)))$; there exists a generator $\varpi\ne0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_n(Q,n)$, an element $f$ of the compositum lies in `R.integers` precisely when $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_n(Q,n)$ with $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$, and for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ transported along $\varphi_n(Q,n)\circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ satisfies $f\cdot h=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   Furthermore the layers are compatible: there is a proof that $K_n\le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q,n)\le S_n(Q,n')$, and, with respect to it, $K_n\le K_{n'}$ implies that $S_n(Q,n')$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ have one and the same image in $\bar F$ for all $n,n'$; and $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricted to $S_n(Q,n)$ agrees with $\chi_n(Q,n)$ whenever $K_n\le K_{n'}$.
--
--   The layer discs satisfy the same three global properties as in the hypothesis: for $Q,Q'\notin N$ and any layer $n$, a place $P$ lying in both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$ forces $Q=Q'$; for $Q\notin N$, any $n$ and any $P\in D_n(Q,n)$, the order at $P$ of the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` in $\bar F$ is $\ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving `R.integers`, the action of `R.resAut τ hτ` preserves $N$, and for $Q\notin N$ and every $n$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n) = Dn (R.resAut τ hτ • Q) n`.
--
--   Finally, the two linking conjuncts: for every $Q\notin N$ and every layer $n$, $S_b(Q)\le S_n(Q,n)$; and every place $P\in D_b(Q)$ lies in $D_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   This is the propagation step in the construction of the semistable chart data for the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a place of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ above $q$: smooth-point stalks (étale coordinate rings with residue character, and their residue discs) already constructed over the base layer $k_0$ are extended to every finite layer $K_n$ over the same end set $N$, with the base stalks and base discs contained in the layer ones. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes), where the ends and the residue discs must be compared across layers.
